From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 13:56:36 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: extend the LAN MAC range to the 16-address block

The FE treats a LAN frame as routed only when its destination MAC is
in the LAN range. The driver builds that range from the MACs of the
GDM ports. On SmartOS the LAN bridge uses base + 1, which is outside
the range. The PPE then learned routed LAN traffic as L2 bridge flows,
and LAN to WAN flows were never offloaded.

The LAN range now covers the whole block of 16 addresses that SmartOS
assigns, base to base + 15. The rule is static, because SmartOS always
assigns the block from a base that ends in 0.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c |    7 +++++++
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h |    1 +
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -140,6 +140,13 @@ static int airoha_set_macaddr(struct air
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
 
+	/* SmartOS gives each device 16 addresses from a base that ends in 0.
+	 * LAN hosts use base + 1 to base + 15 (bridges, Wi-Fi BSSIDs) as the
+	 * router address, and those are not the addresses of the GDM ports.
+	 */
+	if (airoha_is_lan_gdm_dev(dev))
+		lmax = max(lmax, lmin | AIROHA_LAN_MAC_BLOCK_MASK);
+
 	reg = airoha_is_lan_gdm_dev(dev) ? REG_FE_LAN_MAC_H : REG_FE_WAN_MAC_H;
 	val = (addr[0] << 16) | (addr[1] << 8) | addr[2];
 	airoha_fe_wr(eth, reg, val);
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h
@@ -78,6 +78,7 @@
 #define MTK_HDR_XMIT_TAGGED_TPID_88A8	2
 #define AIROHA_HEADROOM (NET_SKB_PAD + NET_IP_ALIGN)
 #define AIROHA_MAC_ADDR_NUM		7
+#define AIROHA_LAN_MAC_BLOCK_MASK	0xf
 enum {
 	QDMA_INT_REG_IDX0,
 	QDMA_INT_REG_IDX1,
